15 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating article selection for a review: from 6629 database articles and 68 conference records, 6562 were excluded by title and abstract, leaving 135 full texts. After further exclusion of 66 articles for reasons such as distant metastasis, reviews, comments, lack of full text, surgery post-treatment, non-English language, insufficient data, ongoing experiments, or other reasons, 30 single-arm trials and 39 controlled trials remained. Trials are grouped by treatment types including ICT-CCRT, CCRT-cIO, CCRT-IO, CT-CCRT, and CCRT-CT, each with their counts of single-arm and controlled trials.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Forest plot graphic consisting of two panels labeled A and B, each showing meta-analysis results comparing various cancer treatment regimens. Individual studies are listed with hazard ratios and confidence intervals, grouped by intervention type. Diamonds indicate pooled summary estimates, with horizontal axis centered at one to represent no effect. Study weights and heterogeneity statistics are reported for each subgroup.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Heatmap-style matrix comparing treatments for progression-free survival versus overall survival in cancer therapy. Cells show hazard ratios and confidence intervals; bold values indicate statistical significance. Blue background highlights specific treatment comparisons.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Network diagrams labeled A and B each contain six nodes connected to a central node labeled CCRT, with other nodes labeled CCRT-IO, CT-CCRT, ICT-CCRT, CCRT-CT, and CCRT-cIO. Thick blue lines represent strong or significant connections between nodes, while thin lines show weaker or less direct relationships. All nodes are represented as orange circles, and layout is consistent between both diagrams.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
